{{template "top.gohtml" .}}

<h1>Logger app — Configuration</h1>
<p class="note">Logger.log pushes to the bundled Loki service on the compose
network — <code>http://loki:3100</code>, no authentication, nothing to
configure beyond the toggle. Strict mode: an unreachable Loki halts the run,
exactly like a broken relay. User log entries live only in Loki; the Logs
page shows this app's own operational file, never Loki.</p>

<form method="post" action="/admin/logger" class="card">
  <label><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" {{if .Logger.Enabled}}checked{{end}} /> Enable the logger app</label>

  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save logger settings</button>
</form>

{{template "bottom.gohtml" .}}
